00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
you might not guess it from the  silhouette but a mandalorian's armor is  as unique as their fingerprints  handed down through generations the  distinctive armor is a defining trait of  the mandalorian people and their culture  this is the history of mandalorian armor  explained  the mandalorians are a nomadic people  but they're not a species  anyone can be a mandalorian if they  practice the tenets of their faith  before the mandalorian boba fett was one  of the most well-known mandalorians in  the star wars universe  but although he wore mandalorian armor  he didn't really grow up in the culture  and therefore is not a true mandalorian  because mandalorians are a war-like  people who often act as mercenaries  wearing armor is one of the six actions  central to their identity  according to star wars novelist karen  travis the other five are speaking the  mandalorian language  contributing to the welfare of their  clan defending themselves and their  families  raising their children as mandalorians  and rallying around the sole leader of  their people  the mandalore when asked yet even though  their armor is a central part of their  culture  mandalorians like reminding each other  that what's inside matters most  a warrior is more than his armor is one  popular mandalorian  saying early mandalorian armor appeared  during season 2 of the animated series  star wars the clone wars  the episode the mandalore plot showed a  mural depicting  ancient mandalorian crusaders wearing  helmets over their cloaks  as they fought the jedi knights to  battle the forced powers of the jedi  the mandalorians modified their fighting  style and weaponry  clone wars director dave filoni once  told comicbook.com  the mandalorian jedi war that i have in  my mind is very much derived from the  oldest  style of thinking of mandalorians which  was that their weapons  their arsenal their technology had a  massive increase once they collided with  the jedi  and found these force-wielding people  that had abilities they didn't  understand  filoni continued their armor is a  reaction to the jedi  and i've always believed that because  that seemed to be something that would  be in the dna  of the joe johnston designs of them as  supercommandos  johnston who directed captain america  the first avenger and the rocketeer  was a concept artist on the original  star wars trilogy  incidentally filoni became the  showrunner on the animated series star  wars rebels  and is now a writer and director on the  mandalorian  both star wars the clone wars and star  wars rebels delve  into other mandalorian armor history  tied to the mandalorian civil war  which split the group into the pacifist  new mandalorians  and the militant death watch although  many fans would recognize a mandalorian  by their armor  specifically the full-face helmet with  t-shaped visor  this schism revealed other variations  particularly in the helmets  for instance the female warriors of  death watch known as the night owls  wore helmets with eye slits that would  tilt up like an owls  sabine wren the star wars rebels  character who is a mandalorian warrior  and demolitions expert has a night owls  helmet that she inherited  speaking of sabine she doesn't follow  the strict helmet rules that denjarin  outlines on the mandalorian  namely that he can't remove his helmet  in front of other people or his vow is  broken and he's no longer part of his  tribe  sabine often goes without her helmet  even though she usually wears her armor  a mandalorian's armor includes a lot of  accessories  the helmet for instance has a comb link  with an antenna it also includes night  vision  a tactical display facial and vocal  recognition  a fingerprint scanner video recording  links to vehicles and weapons  and flight controls for the jet packs  that mandalorians use to be more  maneuverable in battle  in the mandalorian den jaren receives a  jet pack from the armorer at the end of  season 1  which he uses to fight against moth  gideon mando fares pretty well  considering that he's still learning the  controls unlike the undignified  trajectory of boba fett  in star wars return of the jedi one key  part of the mandalorians arsenal is the  van brace  a wrist gauntlet chock full of various  weaponry  including a 25 meter long retractable  fiber cord  flamethrower energy shield protector  trackers  laser targeting sights launchers for  tranquilizing or explosive darts  a mini rocket launcher motion detectors  repulsors  a communication system and a touchscreen  display next to its well-known  silhouette mandalorian armor is  also known for its toughness thanks to  best car a material that's also  called mandalorian iron or mandalorian  steel  vescar protects against blaster shots as  well as lightsaber strikes but it's also  lightweight  allowing the wearers to be much more  agile than say tony stark learning to  fly in his mark 1 suit in 2008's iron  man  okay this is where i don't want to be  yikes bheskar has such remarkable  strength because of both its natural  properties  and mandalorian metalworking techniques  dinjarin causes a stir when a client  pays him in bars of vesgar  another mandalorian remembers how the  rare metal could be mined  only on their home planet of mandalore  and was likely stolen during the great  purge  in the mandalorian's first episode the  armorer uses a bar of best guard to  forge a new pauldron  or shoulder plate fermando the colors  and markings on mandalorian armor can be  highly varied and are often used to  express lineage or state of mind  according to travis that said  mandalorians also decorate their armor  according to taste  they'll repaint their armor if they  change clans or if they're on a  particular task  sabine wren for instance often changed  her armor's markings much like she  changed her hair color  adding a prominent insignia in her  starboard design a precursor to the  emblem of the rebel alliance  blue and green are popular armor colors  for mandalorians who like to be  conspicuous  travis wrote referencing another  mandalorian saying it's one thing to see  us coming  and another to do something about it  mandalorian armor doesn't just provide  protection  it's also an heirloom because bhaskar  can last for hundreds of years  as sabine wren once said the armor i  wear  is 500 years old i reforged it to my  liking but the battles  the history the blood all lives within  it and the same goes for every  mandalorian  travis explained in star wars insider  that as a nomadic people mandalorians  frugally invested much of their wealth  into their armor and weapons  this was certainly practical because  they could take their earnings with them  early in the mandalorian mando receives  a large payment of besgar  after delivering the child to the  mysterious imperial client  after mando presents the best guard to  the armorer she suggests that she can  craft a full queer rasp for him  plus whistling birds a type of mini  missile the excess he donates to the  foundlings  the orphaned children the mandalorians  protect catching up afterward with grief  karga head of the bounty hunter's guild  mando draws  several stairs over his shiny new  threads but he's really just following  the investment strategy of ancient  mandalorians  besides cargo notes the grumblers are  just jealous that they didn't get all  that loot  mandalorians love personalized armor  sabine wren  embraced this part of mandalorian  culture throughout star wars rebels  and not just through her signature  design rebels fans know that she kept  the armor's insulating body glove but  stripped away a lot of the other pieces  for maximum mobility  she also upgraded her helmet's  electronics although she used the video  and image recording abilities to capture  her artwork much more than the targeting  viewfinder  on the mandalorian the armorer has  strikingly distinctive armor  from the fur across the back plate to  the shape of her eyes on her helmet  polygon notes that her helmet also  appears to have  zebrak horns which could be a reference  to darth maul  a zabrak who briefly ruled mandalore and  headed the death watch on star wars the  clone wars  mandalorian armor often has sigils or  symbols painted on the chest plate or  helmet indicating their lineage  allegiance or even awards for bravery  according to travis  the armor can also have a signet  specifying the wearer's particular clan  when the mandalorian begins din jaren  has no signet  even though he was adopted by the  mandalorians as an orphan  was trained as a warrior and joined  their tribe he starts the first season  as a classic western lone wolf archetype  that changes once he meets the child who  uses his  force powers to help den defeat a  charging mudhorn a creature that  resembles a gigantic rhino  when the armorer suggests that he has  earned the mudhorn as a signet for  failing the creature he declines  saying that it wasn't a noble kill but  once den has a change of heart and  retrieves the child from the imperials  who want his power  the armorer decides that den is worthy  of such an honor  she forges a mudhorn signet for him and  instructs him to take care of the green  foundling and to return the child to his  own  kind if possible in the meantime she  says  you are a clan of two check out one of  our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about star wars  are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

